1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,526
A recall alert can reach a clinic in seconds.

2
00:00:03,526 --> 00:00:05,876
But it cannot inspect a stockroom.

3
00:00:05,876 --> 00:00:09,010
Someone still needs to find the right lot,

4
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:12,535
resolve missing labels, and account for every affected unit.

5
00:00:12,535 --> 00:00:16,453
Lotline turns that unfinished work into a clear response record.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,357
Sign in with an email account to use your own inventory.

7
00:00:26,357 --> 00:00:27,941
The workspace starts empty.

8
00:00:27,941 --> 00:00:31,110
Import a stock CSV, review the original recall

9
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:34,675
notice, and approve its exact product and lot scope.

10
00:00:34,675 --> 00:00:39,428
Your records are saved to your account, separately from the sample demo.

11
00:00:39,428 --> 00:00:41,408
No patient information is needed.

12
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,362
For this walkthrough, we will switch to fictional sample stock.

13
00:00:52,362 --> 00:00:54,979
Sixty-four units match the reviewed recall.

14
00:00:54,979 --> 00:00:57,160
Twelve have no recorded lot.

15
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:59,777
Thirty are outside this specific scope.

16
00:00:59,777 --> 00:01:03,266
Those twelve unknown units stay open for investigation.

17
00:01:03,266 --> 00:01:05,883
Missing information never becomes an all-clear.

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,247
The source snapshot shows exactly what was reviewed: one product,

19
00:01:13,247 --> 00:01:17,070
one lot, and instructions authorizing return to the supplier.

20
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:20,892
Lotline can look up FDA references, but a person

21
00:01:20,892 --> 00:01:24,714
must verify the current notice and approve the scope.

22
00:01:24,714 --> 00:01:27,687
The software does not invent removal instructions.

23
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,266
Here, a stockroom check confirms that all twelve unlabelled records belong to the affected lot.

24
00:01:36,266 --> 00:01:40,444
We enter the package identifier and retain a verification reference.

25
00:01:40,444 --> 00:01:45,875
Saving the check updates the assessment to seventy-six affected units, with zero unresolved.

26
00:01:45,875 --> 00:01:49,217
Every change is recorded in the activity history.

27
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,631
Now the response moves from identification to accountability.

28
00:01:57,631 --> 00:02:01,262
For each affected stock record, we enter the

29
00:02:01,262 --> 00:02:04,893
quantity placed in quarantine and the supporting reference.

30
00:02:04,893 --> 00:02:08,979
Then we record the supplier return and its receipt.

31
00:02:08,979 --> 00:02:14,425
The server prevents disposition from exceeding quarantine, and quarantine from exceeding stock.

32
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:16,695
Repeated submissions cannot double-count units.

33
00:02:16,695 --> 00:02:20,326
These are fictional actions for this demonstration; in

34
00:02:20,326 --> 00:02:24,411
use, staff must verify the physical handling and evidence.

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,153
Once all seventy-six affected units have disposition records, completion becomes available.

36
00:02:43,153 --> 00:02:48,775
A reviewer must confirm inventory coverage, notice amendments, and the final records.

37
00:02:48,775 --> 00:02:51,118
Completing the response locks it.

38
00:02:51,118 --> 00:02:54,865
This closes the local stock response; it does

39
00:02:54,865 --> 00:02:59,082
not terminate a regulatory recall or certify product safety.

40
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,424
The evidence packet brings the source, reviewed scope, stock assessment, actions, and activity together.

41
00:03:08,424 --> 00:03:13,472
Download JSON or a reconciliation CSV, or print the response record.

42
00:03:13,472 --> 00:03:15,766
Checksums help verify file consistency.

43
00:03:15,766 --> 00:03:19,437
The same account and workflow work on a

44
00:03:19,437 --> 00:03:23,567
phone, so records remain accessible where the stock is.

45
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,535
Lotline is created by Shivam Gupta for the practical

46
00:03:29,535 --> 00:03:33,069
work between a recall alert and a documented response.

47
00:03:33,069 --> 00:03:38,174
Try the sample demo, or sign in and test your own nonpatient inventory.

48
00:03:38,174 --> 00:03:40,138
Every unit needs an answer.
